Z||000000||beachbomb||07-22-2001||02:54 PM||||Hi all, i'm replacing my cam timing gear, oil pump, water pump etc, and i was wondering, do you use the RTV gasket maker on all of these or should i use the original type gaskets for them, or both, plmk, i wasn't sure if you could put a gasket on and use RTV on it as well, if so how, thanks..jim||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cozmo||07-22-2001||03:32 PM||||Well I hope the job is going well, Jim.<BR>I used both the gasket and RTV when I reassembled mine, but I didn't drop the oil pan.  Result? it leaks bad. Sounds like you should have better success since you'll be sealing the oil pan and timing cover at the same time.<BR>Maybe somebody else on the forum has a trick way to seal that area right.  It seems like a poor design to me.<BR>Good Luck <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
